A destroy zeroes a ready thread but leaves it on the run queue.
The next switch would run memory that is no longer a thread;
the run queue holds only live threads.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: queue holds something that is not a thread

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -219,4 +219,2 @@ void sched_forget_pool(struct pool *pool)
                 unwait(t);
-            } else if (t->state == THREAD_READY) {
-                ring_remove(&run_queue, t);
             }
